Stage 8: the core-ffi arm. M1, encode and decode, through the real C ABI.

commit:    1f439b1353cdaa6562097c70699b82941c815af3 (+ this slice)
core:      ffi/poc/rust/target/release/libak_core.so, the SAME artifact the Rust
           slice loads. Not a second core: one native core with N bindings is the
           proposal, so the C# arm binds to it rather than reimplementing it.
binding:   generated, ffi/poc/csharp/gen/cs_abi.py + cs_coreffi.py
linkage:   shared library, P/Invoke via LibraryImport, reverse calls via
           [UnmanagedCallersOnly] with the abort guard (R7: linkage is part of
           the mechanism and a C++ host that statically links pays a direct call)
strings:   STAGED as UTF-8 and handed over as data with tc = ak_tc_bytes(), which
           is a function pointer INTO THE CORE and crosses nothing. The alternative
           ak_str offers, a host transcoder callback, is one reverse crossing per
           string: 5 per ResultRaw, 5,000 for P1.2, at .NET's 7.5-12 ns. Not built.
R13:       the Rust crossing benchmark measures 1.8 ns forward on this container.

SCOPE. M1 only. ResultRaw is a leaf, which is the simplest end-to-end path and
the one that isolates the interface cost from the batching predicate refusing
anything. M2 to M7 are NOT built; TaskDetailed is not a leaf and that is where
the predicate starts refusing, which is a different measurement.

